r for mass spectrometry mzXML, mzData and mzML files. The package contains the original code written by the ISB, and a subset of the proteowizard library for mzML and mzIdentML. The netCDF reading code has previously been used in XCMS.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:01:32Z","last_update_date":"2019-07-20T17:08:39Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["2.8.0"],"collections":["BioConductor","Proteomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:mzr","credit":[{"email":"b.fischer@dkfz.de","name":"Bernd Fischer","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"lg390@cam.ac.uk","name":"Laurent Gatto","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"qkou@umail.iu.edu","name":"Qiang Kou","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"sneumann@ipb-halle.de","name":"Steffen Neumann","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/mzR.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Formatting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0335"}]}],"name":"mzR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btn323","metadata":{"abstract":"The ProteoWizard software project provides a modular and extensible set of open-source, cross-platform tools and libraries. The tools perform proteomics data analyses; the libraries enable rapid tool creation by providing a robust, pluggable development framework that simplifies and unifies data file access, and performs standard proteomics and LCMS dataset computations. The library contains readers and writers of the mzML data format, which has been written using modern C++ techniques and design principles and supports a variety of platforms with native compilers. The software has been specifically released under the Apache v2 license to ensure it can b